WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.511
Command and control means unauthorized communication that allows an affected asset, account, workload, or service to receive direction or send

2
00:00:08.661 --> 00:00:10.861
status outside normal trust boundaries.

3
00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:19.096
Defenders should treat this stage as a question about communication evidence, not as a lesson in setup or evasion.

4
00:00:19.246 --> 00:00:26.480
Useful signals may appear in DNS logs, proxy logs, firewall records, endpoint telemetry, cloud network flow records,

5
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.183
identity events, or SaaS activity logs.

6
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.533
The details vary by environment.

7
00:00:31.683 --> 00:00:39.343
A workstation, a container workload, a cloud function, and a compromised account may all create different communication patterns.

8
00:00:39.493 --> 00:00:46.301
Defensive controls include egress filtering, destination allowlists, segmentation, proxy inspection, anomaly detection, and rapid containment paths.

9
00:00:46.451 --> 00:00:52.409
Analysts should ask what communicated, where it communicated, how often, through which control point,

10
00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:55.963
and whether that behavior matches expected business activity.

11
00:00:56.113 --> 00:00:58.666
Containment decisions should be evidence based.

12
00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:05.624
Isolating a host, disabling a credential, blocking a destination, or segmenting a workload can reduce risk,

13
00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:09.179
but those actions should be recorded and coordinated.

14
00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:16.988
The value of this stage is to make outbound visibility and containment planning part of normal defensive readiness.

15
00:01:17.138 --> 00:01:23.096
This stage is a reminder that outbound visibility matters as much as inbound defense.

16
00:01:23.246 --> 00:01:30.480
If the organization cannot explain which systems can reach which destinations, containment becomes slower and less precise.

17
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:35.736
Well-governed egress makes unusual communication easier to notice and easier to limit.
